// M8d exit scenario (plan docs/plans/M8D-ENGINEERS.md §8 #9): a deliberate breach. Blue attacks
// the uplands village through a Red obstacle belt: a minefield across the whole western approach
// (FM 20-32 turn-effect density) with triple-standard wire in front of it on the direct line,
// covered by fire from the village 800 m behind it (FM 90-7: obstacles covered by fire). Blue's
// lead platoons each have a mine plough or roller tank (default ON OBSTACLE: BREACH). The way round
// to the north is long; without the kits the attack must take it. The Blue AI plan is used only
// when the side is not player-controlled (headless runs, tests).
(
    id: "m8d-deliberate-breach",
    name: "DELIBERATE BREACH",
    date: (1990, 5, 10),
    start_time_s: 25200, // 07:00
    map: (id: "uplands", recipe: "wooded-uplands", seed: 7, size_m: 8000.0),
    seed: 1,
    briefing: "SITUATION: TWO RED TANK PLATOONS AND TWO BMPS HOLD THE VILLAGE. RECCE REPORTS A MINEFIELD AND WIRE ABOUT 800 M WEST OF IT, RUNNING NORTH FROM THE SOUTHERN EDGE OF THE MAP FOR ABOUT 3 KM. A 155 MM BATTERY (ARTY 1) IS IN DIRECT SUPPORT.\n\nMISSION: 1ST AND 2ND PLATOONS BREACH THE BELT AND SEIZE THE VILLAGE WITHIN 60 MINUTES. 1-1 HAS A MINE PLOUGH, 2-1 A MINE ROLLER: THEIR PLATOONS BREACH (ON OBSTACLE: BREACH), THE OTHERS BYPASS.\n\nNOTES: SUPPRESS AND OBSCURE BEFORE YOU REDUCE: OVERWATCH THE VILLAGE FROM THE HIGH GROUND, SMOKE THE BREACH, CALL FIRE ON THE DEFENDERS. THE LANE IS 4.5 M WIDE: TANKS GO THROUGH IN COLUMN. A SIDE THAT LOSES 70 % OF ITS VEHICLES LOSES.",
    objectives: [(name: "VILLAGE", centre: (4380.0, 1000.0), radius_m: 300.0)],
    victory: (time_limit_s: 3600.0, objective: "VILLAGE", attacker: 0, destroyed_fraction: 0.7),
    sides: [
        (
            name: "BLUE",
            doctrine: "western-combined",
